Z||000000||jlhuber||09-08-2000||09:41 AM||||i found a formula for sale in my area last night, and i just can't pass a fiero that is for sale without stoping and taking a gander.  i am curious, though, as to what all you value gurus would put as an approxamite price on her.  here are the stats:<P>1988 fiero formula, sunroof, factory birght red paint, has a few nicks and scratches, front fascia (sp?) could use some fresh paint, lt. grey cloth interior, automatic, runs great, driver's seat is torn, drivers seatbelt won't retract, both headlights go up & down fast, new rack & pinion, new rear manifold (not installed yet)  it does have 134,000 (yes one hundred and thirty four thousand) miles though.  owner is asking $2200 for it, do you guys think he is crazy?<P>the car is in good shape, except for the signs of aging that a 12yr old daily driver is going to have.  i am going this afternoon to take her for a spin and to check it out a little better now that it is daylight.  it is located in wrightstown, nj right outside mcguire air force base.  i am thinking of buying it to finish my project that i had started but had to abort very suddenly.  if anyone else is interested and wants the address of the seller let me know.  ||||reg||5
